  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated and Inclusive Humanitarian WASH and Protection Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam proposes a two -phased emergency response that directly improves the conditions in areas of (re)displacement and return for 45,966 vulnerable women, men, boys, and girls. It will target districts in Kirkuk (Daquq, Hawija, and Kirkuk) and Ninewa (Telafar, Sinjar, Ba&apos;aj, and Hatra) Governorates for 24 and 18 months, respectively. Local partner Rehabilitation, Education and Community Health (REACH) will deliver Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and Protection activities in Kirkuk, with the exception of activities directly implemented by Oxfam in Kirkuk District. Sewan Women&apos;s Empowerment organisation (SEWAN) will deliver all Protection activities in Ninewa. Integrated WASH and protection components will be supported by Oxfam&apos;s Country Humanitarian Team (CHT)  - a mobile rapid assessment and response mechanism.  Since 2020, the deployed CHT has responded to COVID -19 and camp closures, supporting tens of thousands of vulnerable House Holds (HHs) with COVID -19 supplies and winterization kits across five governorates.</narrative>
  </description>
